# Installation

## Check your version of python

You will need python 3.11 or later. You can check your version of python by
typing into a terminal:

```
$ python3 --version
```

## Create the environment

It is recommended that you install into an isolated environment so this
installation will not interfere with any existing Python software:

{% if is_uv %}
```
$ uv sync                      # create .venv and install everything (incl. dev deps)
```
{% elif is_poetry %}
```
$ poetry install                # create .venv and install everything (incl. dev deps)
```
{% else %}
```
$ pixi install                  # create the pixi environment (dev feature included)
```
{% endif %}

## Installing the library

You can now install the library and its dependencies:

{% if is_uv %}
```
$ pip install {{distribution_name}}
```
{% elif is_poetry %}
```
$ poetry add {{distribution_name}}
```
{% else %}
```
# pixi project - the environment is managed by pixi
$ pixi install
```
{% endif %}

If you require a feature that is not currently released you can also install
from github:

{% if is_uv %}
```
$ pip install git+{{repo_url}}.git
```
{% elif is_poetry %}
```
$ poetry add git+{{repo_url}}.git
```
{% else %}
```
# pixi project - the environment is managed by pixi
$ pixi install
```
{% endif %}

The library should now be installed and the commandline interface on your path.
You can check the version that has been installed by typing:

```
$ {{repo_name}} --version
```
